Z||000000||ChopTop||03-04-2001||01:01 PM||||In the March issue of Sports Compact Car a auto show is being sponserd by their sister publication Import Tuner.  The event is being held at Houston Raceway Park, Houston, TX, for June 8-10, 2001.  There is a domestic show class.  Also, the NOPI Nationals is being held at the Atlanta Speedway in Atlanta, GA, on September 15 & 16, 2001.  Nopi is also holding two other regional shows (see NOPI.com for location & dates).  I believe they also have domestic classes but could not find classes on their website.  Unfortunately, none of these shows are within a reasonable distance for me to attend (not that I would enter since my car is no where near being ready).  However, I was wondering if any list members plan to enter these import dominated functions?  I think it would be a excellent venue for Fiero owners to show our cars are ideal cars to own and modify.  Anyone up to the challenge?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Sleeper||03-04-2001||01:15 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ChopTop:<BR><B>In the March issue of Sports Compact Car a auto show is being sponserd by their sister publication Import Tuner.  The event is being held at Houston Raceway Park, Houston, TX, for June 8-10, 2001.  There is a domestic show class.  Also, the NOPI Nationals is being held at the Atlanta Speedway in Atlanta, GA, on September 15 & 16, 2001.  Nopi is also holding two other regional shows (see NOPI.com for location & dates).  I believe they also have domestic classes but could not find classes on their website.  Unfortunately, none of these shows are within a reasonable distance for me to attend (not that I would enter since my car is no where near being ready).  However, I was wondering if any list members plan to enter these import dominated functions?  I think it would be a excellent venue for Fiero owners to show our cars are ideal cars to own and modify.  Anyone up to the challenge?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I went to the SEMA/NOPI west coast nationals last month. it was awesome alot of sweet cars domestic and imports but as you say "import dominated functions"...but no fieros Eric at west coast fiero said they were there but i didn't see them. i think there was a Fiero that won a award at the east coast NOPI show last year, some other ppl on here would know more info about that though. all in all NOPI usually put son great shows, if modified fieros competed i think they would give other cars a run for their money, easily. but...i just go to these shows for the chicks anyway. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>85 GT<BR>17" Racing Hart C5 wheels, Kumho Ecsta Supra 712 tires, Intrax lowering spring, KYB shocks, KYB-GR2 struts, Chris West's Strut Tower Bar, J.E.T. super chip, Accel Super Coil, Accel Wires, K&N filter and Optima Battery.||||reg||1
